{"id":1129,"level":80,"name":"Форсовані взяття","group":"Форсування","format":27,"description":"<p>In the previous exercise, you learned how to exchange pieces as part of a forcing combination. A simple winning move concluded a series of forcing moves.<br /><br />We will now look at another type of exchanging: <em>sacrificing</em>. With a sacrifice you give up material with the goal of getting something else (something more valuable!) in return. Why wouldn&rsquo;t you give your opponent a present if you can win a queen?<br /><br />Look at the example. White exchanges a rook for a knight. That&rsquo;s not a very good exchange. But on the next move White can win a rook in a double attack. All in all, White&nbsp;out on top.<br /><br />Remember: always look out for forcing combinations. And don&rsquo;t forget to think about sacrifices as well as ordinary exchanges!<br /><br /><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Win material by means of a forcing capture (sacrifice).</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":97,"examples":[{"fen":"5k2/1pr3p1/1N3p1p/1Rn5/p7/P6P/1P3PP1/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Rxc5 Rxc5 2. Nd7+ Ke7 3. Nxc5 1-0","text":"<p>Білі можуть виграти за допомогою гарної комбінації! Пожертвувавши власну туру, білі отримують можливість виконати вилку наступним ходом.</p>","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":39364,"fen":"r4bkr/ppp3pp/2nqb3/3n4/2Bp4/5Q2/PPP2PPP/RNB1R1K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Rxe6 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":51258,"fen":"4k3/1bR1b3/1p6/nP3p1p/P5pP/6P1/5B1K/8 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Ra5,Rb7]} 1. Bxb6 (1. Kg1?  ) (1. Bd4?  ) (1. Be3?  ) 1... Bb4 2. Bxa5 ( 2. Bc5?  ) (2. Bd4?  ) 2... Bxa5 3. Rxb7 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":50126,"fen":"8/2p2ppp/2k5/8/4n3/4PP2/3r2PP/3NK2R b K - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Re1,Rh1]} 1... Rxd1+ 2. Kxd1 Nf2+ 3. Kc2 Nxh1 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":44955,"fen":"r3k2r/pp1b1pp1/4p3/q2nP3/5PP1/2P2NKB/P1NPQp